<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Expand <m>{{\left(x+2\right)}^3}</m> by multiplying out brackets. Collect like terms.</p><div><fillin characters="30" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p><m>{{\left(x+2\right)}^3}</m> means <m>{3}</m> factors of <m>({x+2})</m> multiplied together, never <m>{x^3+8}</m>. Multiply two brackets, collect like terms, then multiply by the next bracket.</p><p>First, <m>({x+2})^2 = {x^2+4 x+4}</m>. Multiply this by <m>({x+2})</m>:</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>\times</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{x^2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4 x}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{x}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{x^3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4 x^2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4 x}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2 x^2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8 x}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Collecting like terms, <m>({x+2})^3 = {x^3+6 x^2+12 x+8}</m>.</p><p>The coefficients come from the row 1, 3, 3, 1. Check: putting <m>x = 1</m> gives <m>{3}^{3} = {27}</m> on both sides.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>x^3+6 x^2+12 x+8</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>